    "result_text": "Green. Both findings addressed; acceptance behaviour unchanged.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with both findings \u2014 they match the codebase's clear idiom (branching, rule-bearing derivations get a named, Javadoc'd home like `MembershipLevel.of` / `Regions.localityOf`).\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 logic in the wrong unit:** Extracted the derivation into a new `ContactPreference.of(Owner)` factory returning `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`, and reduced the mapping to `expression = \"java(ContactPreference.of(owner))\"` \u2014 mirroring the `Regions.localityOf(...)` line right above it.\n- I placed it in the **mapper** package (beside `Regions`) rather than the model (beside `MembershipLevel`), because it references the generated `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`. `MembershipLevel` lives in the model precisely because it returns a plain `int` and stays free of any `rest.dto` dependency; putting an enum-returning helper there would have pulled a DTO import into the model layer. This keeps each helper beside the peer whose dependencies it shares.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 duplicated predicate:** Added `Owner.hasEmail()` as the single source of truth for \"email present\" (`email != null && !email.isBlank()`), then pointed both `MembershipLevel.of` and the new `ContactPreference.of` at it, removing the verbatim duplication.\n\nFiles touched:\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 new `hasEmail()` with Javadoc.\n- `MembershipLevel.java` \u2014 now calls `owner.hasEmail()`.\n- `mapper/ContactPreference.java` \u2014 new factory.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 mapping delegates to the factory.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 unchanged from before (the review found it fine).\n\nFull `mvn test` build is green (2/2 passing).",
